# Token Distribution & Vesting Simulator

A Python simulator that models monthly circulating supply, supply inflation and supply-driven sell pressure over 48 months, applied first to a fictional protocol and then to Arbitrum (ARB).

**Headline finding:** in ARB, almost all insider supply unlocks in a single month (month 12: +77.9% circulating supply), so the same sell assumptions produce a sharper one-month price hit than in a protocol with gradual unlocks.

## What it does

- Models token allocation buckets with a TGE unlock, a cliff lump and linear vesting
- Builds a 48-month circulating supply curve and monthly inflation rate
- Estimates supply-driven price pressure under three insider sell scenarios (Low, Base, High)
- Applies the same model to real Arbitrum allocation and vesting data
- Compares ARB, OP and DYDX as structural risk patterns

