## Model design

Each allocation bucket has five parameters: `pct` (share of supply), `tge` (fraction unlocked at launch), `cliff` (cliff month), `lump` (fraction released at the cliff) and `vest` (months of linear vesting after the cliff).

Unlocked fraction at month t = `tge` + `lump` (if t >= cliff) + (1 - `tge` - `lump`) x min(max(t - cliff, 0), `vest`) / `vest`

Circulating supply is the sum across buckets. Inflation is the month-over-month percentage change.

### Sell pressure

For each month:

1. New unlocks = change in each bucket's unlocked tokens
2. Tokens sold = new unlocks x the bucket's sell fraction
3. Pressure = tokens sold / monthly volume, where volume = previous circulating supply x daily turnover x 30
4. Monthly price impact = -K x pressure, compounded into a price index (start = 100)

Assumptions: `TURNOVER` = 3% of float traded daily, `K` = 0.5, demand held constant (this isolates supply effects only).

| Sell fraction | Low | Base | High |
|---|---|---|---|
| Team | 10% | 20% | 50% |
| Investors | 30% | 50% | 70% |
| Community | 25% | 40% | 50% |
| Treasury | 0% | 5% | 10% |
| Future Dev | 5% | 10% | 20% |

For ARB, Team and Investors use the same Low/Base/High rates, Foundation uses 0% / 5% / 10%, and Airdrops are 0% because they unlocked fully at launch.

